  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Finish through contact",
  "description": "The coach (or a player) stands by the basket with a contact pad. Players line up on the wing with a ball each, drive to the basket and finish. As the player goes up, the coach gives a light bump with the pad on the hip or shoulder – never on the arms or in mid-air so that someone could land badly. The player has to hold their line, protect the ball and still score. Switch sides so everyone finishes with both hands.\n\nStart with a two-foot power finish: jump stop on both feet, ball high and go straight up into the contact. Then a regular one-foot lay-up. Variants: a euro step around the coach standing in the way, and a floater over a help defender stepping into the lane.\n\nStart gently with light contact and build up. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Take the contact with your shoulder and hip – not with the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Ball high and tight, two hands for as long as possible."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Jump up, not forward: that keeps your balance when the bump comes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Finish every time – expect to play through the contact."
    }
  ],
